[]($section.id('about'))
# About these notes

Things too small for a blog post: shell snippets, config fragments, links and
random thoughts.

You can [subscribe via RSS]($link.page('notes').alternative('rss')), or browse the
[notes archive]($link.page("notes")) for previous years.

## [Notes are live]($section.id("2026-11-15T12:00:00"))
Each entry is a `##` heading whose title is a link carrying
`$section.id("YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS")`. That id gives the entry its own anchor,
its date, and its `pubDate` in the RSS feed.

```console
$ nix shell nixpkgs#ripgrep
```
